Changes from upstream in this fork:
- Package renamed semantica -> netiegraph, semantica_mcp -> netiegraph_mcp;
  environment variables SEMANTICA_* -> NETIE_GRAPH_*; RDF namespace
  https://semantica.dev/ -> https://netie.ai/graph/.
- Branding and logo replaced with Netie's. "Semantica" is upstream's name and
  is used here only to attribute the origin of the code.
- tests/context/test_drift_search.py uses the entity name "Netie" instead of
  "NetieGraph": its pruning test scores token/substring overlap with a query
  containing "graph", so the anchor name must not contain that word.
- requirements-ci.txt and uv.lock were regenerated with uv (pins identical
  to upstream) instead of carrying upstream's text with the old name.
- Upstream tests fixed in this fork (upstream's CI does not run them, so they
  had gone stale):
  - tests/ingest/test_ingestors.py, tests/ingest/test_web_ingestor.py: mock
    request_with_ssrf_guard, the layer the ingestors fetch through; they
    mocked requests.get/Session.get and so reached the real network.
  - tests/triplet_store/test_jena_store_empty_graph.py: give each thread a
    unique index; thread idents are reused after a thread exits, so threads
    could write the same triple.
- Code fixes (bugs that showed once every pinned extra is installed):
  - netiegraph/vector_store/weaviate_store.py: drop the unused QueryReturn
    import, which does not exist in the pinned weaviate-client 4.16 and so
    made the Weaviate store report "not available" with the client installed;
    resolve Filter through the module's own weaviate reference first.
- Test isolation fixes (upstream's CI runs a few subsets, never the whole
  suite in one process, so cross-test leaks went unseen):
  - tests/conftest.py (new): strip every *_API_KEY from the environment for
    non-integration tests (several LLM tests made live provider calls with
    whatever key the machine had); give each test a fresh extraction config;
    reset the progress-tracker singleton (including its one-way "disabled by
    env" latch) per test; and scope each test module's import-time os.environ
    changes (e.g. NETIE_GRAPH_DISABLE_PROGRESS=1) to that module's own tests.
  - tests/test_huggingface_impl.py: its module-level sys.modules mocks
    (including a MagicMock config module) stayed installed for the rest of
    the session; they are now restored after import and re-applied only
    around this file's tests.
- Test fixes against the pinned dependencies:
  - tests/explorer/test_explorer_entrypoints.py: FastAPI 0.141 mounts
    included routers lazily (no ``route.path``); assert which route serves
    each URL instead, including that an unknown URL reaches the SPA fallback.
  - tests/vector_store/test_faiss_index.py: PQ with bits=4 (faiss-cpu 1.15
    SIMD needs ksub % 8 == 0; bits=2 errors on AVX2).
  - tests/export/test_distance_exporter.py: the "no warning" test counts
    warnings only, not INFO records from other modules.
  - tests/kg/test_integration_comprehensive.py: the performance benchmark
    runs with garbage collection paused (thresholds unchanged); the timed
    work takes ~10 ms, and a collection pause late in a long session pushed
    it past 1 s.
- Upstream project files that name upstream contacts or release history
  (SECURITY, SUPPORT, CHANGELOG, RELEASE_NOTES, CITATION, CODE_OF_CONDUCT,
  CONTRIBUTING, GROWTH) are not carried; see the upstream repository for them.
